14. Prompt versioning – an important production concept
Suppose you update your technical assistant prompt from version 1.0 to version 1.1.
You should be able to identify which prompt version generated a particular response.
Your existing templates.py already contains:
</>Python
"version": "1.0"

When you change the instructions, update it:
</>Python
"version": "1.1"

Your advanced endpoint already returns:
</>Python
{
  "template_name": "technical_assistant",
  "prompt_version": "1.1"
}

In production, persist these fields with each request. This makes it possible to compare response quality between prompt versions.
A good practice is to keep prompt templates in your code repository, review changes through Git, and test prompt changes before deployment. OpenAI also recommends code-managed prompts and evaluation tests for production applications. 
