15. Important configuration correction
Before testing temperature, make your model capability configuration explicit.
In services/model_router.py, use:
</>Python
"supports_temperature": (
    os.getenv("OPENAI_FAST_SUPPORTS_TEMPERATURE", "false").lower()
    == "true"
)

Do the same for the quality entry.
Add this to .env:
</>env
OPENAI_FAST_SUPPORTS_TEMPERATURE=false
OPENAI_QUALITY_SUPPORTS_TEMPERATURE=false

Keep these false unless the selected model supports temperature. If it does, set the appropriate value to true.
For your first tests, use "temperature": null. This avoids sending an unsupported parameter.
